I had intended to make this video on you  know the first of January but I was on a  Christmas break then and I sort of just  delved into a routine of laziness but  we're still close enough to talk about I  think some New Year's resolutions and  the ones I'll share with you today will  be the ones related to my coming year as  a PhD student one thing I want to  improve on that I think is important for  grad students is to read a lot of papers  in my field of research I think that's  sort of really important to stay at the  top of your field and to know what's  going on I know one of my supervisors  said to me that when a student finishes  their PhD or when they're towards the  end the difference between a good and a  bad student is that the good one has  continuously read lots of journal  articles over the course of the last few  years whilst the bad student is trying  to catch up on all that reading so to  avoid being the bad student I do want to  stay up-to-date with what's going on in  my field I think another thing that's  important to think about as a grad  student is the need to publish your own  papers so it really depends on the field  that you're working in but there's kind  of an expectation that you have maybe at  least three or four first author papers  to your name by the end of your PhD  program that would indicate that the  work you've done is novel and is a  significant contribution so I want to  hopefully this year or at least in the  first half of the year as well get my  first published paper out so there's one  I've worked on the manuscript of already  and I hear that the process of maybe  editing and going through a peer review  is quite lengthy so we'll see how that  hopefully I can get that out as soon as  possible a third thing that I want to  remember to do this year is to be brave  so there's a lot of things that I think  can be quite scary about being at the  study of PhD or being a grad student and  that's trying to set up collaborations  emailing people that you don't know and  asking for things doing a lot of  emailing and just also meeting people at  conferences talking to people and really  sort of knowing what to ask for and not  being shy to talk to people that are the  top of their field they're not being  intimidated by them I feel like I was  quite brave last year and I want to  continue that because at least for me  it's not always so easy I feel like I'm  a really shy person and even have a bit  of social anxiety in a lot of settings  but I think the only way to overcome  that at least for me is to continue to  do things that I would consider brave  feel free to share your resolutions for  the year with me whether they're  academic related or personal I'd love to  hear what other people are trying to  work on and I hope you have a great 2018
 

